# Seamless Login via URL Payload

The goal is to provide a way to log a user in directly via a URL containing `UserName`, `Token`, and `timestamp`. We will modify the **existing [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) GET method** to catch this payload. To avoid duplicating code, we will extract the existing session generation code into a **new helper method** so both the [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) method (for seamless) and the [Home](file:///d:/dev/Ayurved/Ayurved_bkp12032026/AyurvedaPortal/Controllers/LoginController.cs#30-69) POST method (for normal login) can share the session setup logic.

